// THE WITNESS THAT KILLED THE FIRE GATE (c038c091, reverted ba1b2e0e).
// Keep this: the next attempt at closing dyncall-tagblind-print-aug2026
// must agree on it BEFORE anything else, and it is not something the
// fixture corpus or any of the six standing gates produced — only
// generation found it, ~15 minutes into the aug08d soak (hz0).
//
// BISECT (worktree build at each commit, hz0's archived campaign
// binaries for the older points):
//   fb622f09  AGREE      (pre-everything)
//   2a35dab6  AGREE      (arity + frame-swallow + tooling)
//   c038c091  DIVERGENCE (the fire gate)
//
// BOTH halves reproduce it INDEPENDENTLY, which is why the commit was
// reverted whole rather than narrowed:
//   gate forced to 1, delivery = absence  -> DIVERGENCE
//   gate active,      delivery = stale    -> DIVERGENCE
//
// MINIMIZED 2026-08-09: 6157 -> 112 bytes, by delta reduction over
// statements and bracketed subexpressions against the property "jit
// trace is a strict PREFIX of the interp trace" (a LOST FIRE, not any
// divergence). The program below is what remains; the original mutant
// is kept verbatim in the `mutant:` line at the end of this header.
//
//   interp: [0:i64:5  1:i64:6]      jit: [0:i64:5]   <- second fire lost
//
// The 112 bytes are all load-bearing. Each of these, alone, makes it
// AGREE:
//   * collapsing f0/h1 to ONE lambda level (`v34 + h1()`), or to a
//     block (`v34 + {let z = h1(); z}`) — the DynCall must sit in a
//     callee body reached through ANOTHER callee (depth >= 2; three
//     levels still diverges)
//   * making h1's body a constant (`|| -> i64 i64:5`) instead of a
//     builtin call — it must be a DynCall
//   * giving that builtin an argument that fires
// NOT needed (all of these were in the mutant and reduce away): the
// modules, `catch`, `?`/`$`, `/?` vs `+`, refs, `let rec`, list/array
// HOFs, the bottoming block the connect lived in. `str::len` is not
// special — `array::len` / `map::len` do it too. f0's OWN argument
// firing does not rescue it (`f0(v34)` with `|x| h1() + x` diverges).
//
// SO: on cycle 1 nothing feeding `str::len` fires, the gate skips the
// dispatch, and the site is supposed to ride its cached 5 through the
// taint cache. In a callee body that cache is the honor-gated site
// word (abi.rs `emit_scalar_taint_cache_claimed`), and only a REGION
// ROOT caller can register the words for reset — an intermediate
// callee cannot, so honor stays 0, the cache never substitutes, the
// taint escapes h1, poisons `v34 + f0()`, and the kernel emits
// nothing. This is the documented "region-root active, elsewhere
// inert" residual from the jul16 v1 fix; before the gate it was
// benign, because the builtin was called and produced 5 again. The
// gate turns a missed ride into a lost value, which is why the
// delivery half diverges on its own: absence -> builtin returns None
// -> pend -> the same unridable taint.
//
